description:
Loads a published dekadal (10-daily) dataset over a time range, aggregates the three dekads of each calendar month into one value with aggregate_temporal_period, and publishes the result as a new monthly GeoZarr dataset.

The default reducer is `mean`, which is the correct monthly value for per-day *rate* variables such as the CLMS GPP/NPP products (units gC/m²/day): it yields the month's average daily value, still in gC/m²/day. (A plain sum of three daily rates would be meaningless. A true monthly accumulation in gC/m²/month would need day-weighting per dekad and is not provided here.)

Usage — run as a process graph (synchronously via POST /result, or as a batch job):

{
  "agg": {
    "process_id": "aggregate_dekadal_to_monthly",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset_id": "clms_gpp_dekad",
      "output_dataset_id": "clms_gpp_monthly",
      "variable": "gpp",
      "temporal_extent": ["2014-01-01", "2025-12-31"]
    },
    "result": true
  }
}
